nirld - Nirmala linker (ld)

Standalone static linker for the Nirmala binutils. One code base handles
both ELF32 and ELF64 relocatable inputs and produces a static ET_EXEC.

Targets
- elf_x86_64 (ELFCLASS64, RELA)
- elf_i386   (ELFCLASS32, REL)
The target is taken from the first object, or forced with -m.

Usage
  nirld [-m elf_x86_64|elf_i386] [-o out] [-e sym|addr] [-Ttext addr]
        [-s] [-L dir] [-l name] [--start-group ... --end-group] files...

Features
- Relocatable objects (.o) and ar archives (.a, GNU and BSD member names)
- Lazy archive member extraction, archive groups
- Strong, weak, common and undefined symbol resolution
- COMDAT groups: duplicates are dropped and aliased to the kept copy
- .init/.text/.fini, .rodata, init/fini/preinit arrays, .data, .got, .bss
- Static GOT for the *GOT* relocation types, no PLT
- Static TLS (local-exec and initial-exec): .tdata/.tbss, PT_TLS, TPOFF and
  GOTTPOFF/TLS_IE/TLS_GOTIE relocations; the runtime sets the thread pointer
- --gc-sections: roots are the entry symbol, -u symbols, init/fini arrays,
  .init/.fini, .eh_frame, SHF_GNU_RETAIN; .eh_frame is kept whole
- Debug sections (.debug_*, .comment) are merged and relocated; -S drops them
- -u SYMBOL, --defsym SYM=NUM|SYM|SYM+N, -Map FILE, -z execstack
- --oformat binary: flat image without headers (use with -Ttext)
- -z noseparate-code: two PT_LOAD segments (R+X with .rodata, R+W)
- --unresolved-symbols=ignore-all
- Linker symbols: __executable_start, etext, edata, end, __bss_start,
  __{preinit,init,fini}_array_{start,end}, _GLOBAL_OFFSET_TABLE_
- Output: three PT_LOAD segments (R+X, R, R+W) plus PT_GNU_STACK, section
  headers, .symtab and .strtab (omitted with -s)
- Default image base: 0x400000 (x86_64), 0x08048000 (i386)

Layout
  segment 0  headers, .init, .text, .fini    R+X
  segment 1  .rodata                         R
  segment 2  .tdata .tbss .preinit_array .init_array .fini_array
             .data .got .bss                 R+W
  .tbss occupies no address space; PT_TLS covers .tdata and .tbss.
-Ttext places the first code byte at the given address and keeps the ELF
headers in the page(s) before it.

Not supported
- Dynamic linking, shared objects, PIE, PLT, linker scripts
- General-dynamic and local-dynamic TLS (compile with
  -ftls-model=local-exec or initial-exec), IFUNC, SHN_XINDEX
- Big-endian objects, compressed debug sections (dropped)
- Relocatable output (-r), .eh_frame_hdr, section merging of SHF_MERGE data

Adding a target
Add a relocation table and a struct machine entry in src/reloc.c. A table
row maps a relocation type to one of the calculations C_ABS, C_PCREL,
C_GOTSLOT, C_GOTSLOTPC, C_GOTOFF or C_GOTPC, with the field size and
overflow check. Set the machine number, class and default base address.

Build and test
  make
  make test                           (assembler tests, needs as, ar, readelf, nm)
  NIRCC=/path/to/nircc make test      (also links nircc output end to end)
Test coverage, for both 64-bit and 32-bit: assembler cases, GCC objects
(-O0/-O2/-fPIC/-fPIE), gc-sections, DWARF via readelf and addr2line, TLS with
a real thread pointer, flat binary, defsym, map file and nircc output.

Source map
  src/main.c    option parsing and link pipeline
  src/link.c    input order, -l lookup, archive groups
  src/obj.c     ELF object and archive reader, COMDAT handling
  src/sym.c     global symbol table and resolution rules
  src/layout.c  output sections, addresses, linker-defined symbols
  src/reloc.c   machine tables, GOT, relocation application
  src/out.c     ELF writer

The host needs a 64-bit unsigned long (LP64). Code is C89.
